<paragraphs><title>Disallowed: Graphing Calculators</title></paragraphs>
<p>A graphing calculator is an advanced type of calculator that can plot and graph functions, often on a dot-matrix display. In addition to the capabilities of a scientific calculator, it can visually represent functions, handle multiple equations simultaneously, and often support programming and the ability to store data or functions.</p>

<p>The following is a non-exhaustive list of scientific calculators that are <alert>not</alert> allowed for use on proctored exams.</p>

